# Build context pruning for the relay Docker build (sync-relay-server/Dockerfile).
# Keep the context small + reproducible: drop build outputs, IDE/VCS, JS deps, secrets.
.git
.github
.gradle
.kotlin
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.DS_Store
**/build
# ⚠ …except the relay fat jar, which the `prebuilt` target COPYs from the context
# (sync-relay-server/Dockerfile). `**/build` above exists to keep the context small; this is the one
# artefact that has to come back, and only when it has been built first.
!sync-relay-server/build/libs/sync-relay-server-all.jar
# ⚠ …and the commerce fat jar, for the same reason (commerce-service/Dockerfile's
# `prebuilt` target). Same rule: only present once you have built it.
!commerce-service/build/libs/commerce-service-all.jar
**/bin
**/.cxx
**/.externalNativeBuild
captures

# Web / JS — the relay build never needs these.
**/node_modules
web/**/dist
# ⚠ …except the built apex SPA, which web/apex/Dockerfile's `prebuilt` target COPYs from
# the context. Both lines are needed: the first re-admits the directory, the second its
# contents (a negation cannot resurrect children of an excluded directory on its own).
!web/apex/dist
!web/apex/dist/**
# The web apps the apex image serves on their own origins need no exception: build-apex-image.sh
# stages them as web/.apps-dist/<id>, which `web/**/dist` does not match (web-app-suite.md F4).
kotlin-js-store
# Generated store screenshots (gitignored; published to R2). The apex image copies store/ for the
# manifests only.
store/*/screenshots

# Local secrets / machine config (never bake into an image).
local.properties
# Deploy env files (ISSUER_SEED, ACME email, …) — keep them out of the build context entirely.
deploy.env
**/deploy.env
**/*.iml
xcuserdata
iosApp
